From: devkit maintainers
Upstream: https://github.com/Kitware/CMake/blob/master/Source/CTest/cmCTestCurl.h
Subject: Store CURLOPT_PROXYTYPE as long for current libcurl

New libcurl exposes CURLPROXY_* as long constants. CURLOPT_PROXYTYPE already
expects a long argument; an enum member rejects these constants in C++ and
also passed the wrong type to the variadic curl_easy_setopt. This works with
older enum constants through their standard conversion to long as well.

--- a/Source/CTest/cmCTestCurl.h
+++ b/Source/CTest/cmCTestCurl.h
@@ -54,3 +54,3 @@
   std::string HTTPProxy;
-  curl_proxytype HTTPProxyType;
+  long HTTPProxyType;
   bool UseHttp10 = false;
